# UI Design System

## Core Principle — Never Hardcode Colors

Always use CSS design token variables. **Never** use `rgba()` transparent overlays or hardcoded hex colors for anything that should adapt to the theme.

| Token | Default Value | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--bg` | `#0f172a` | Page background, label columns, input backgrounds |
| `--surface` | `#1e293b` | Cards, panels, elevated rows |
| `--surface-hover` | `#2d3a4d` | Hover state backgrounds |
| `--border` | `#3b4a60` | All borders — always visible, never subtle |
| `--text` | `#f1f5f9` | Primary text, input values |
| `--text-muted` | `#a8b8cc` | Labels, hints, secondary text |
| `--primary` | `#3b82f6` | Accent, focus rings, hover borders |

```css
/* ❌ WRONG — invisible on dark theme */
background: rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
color: #d8e8f6;

/* ✅ CORRECT — theme-aware and visible */
background: var(--bg);
border: 1px solid var(--border);
color: var(--text);
```

## Two-Tone Properties Panel Pattern

For any horizontal label + control form (settings, request forms, config panels):

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ [Label col: var(--bg)] │ [Control area: var(--surface)]      │
│ [Label col: var(--bg)] │ [input: var(--bg) + var(--border)]  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- **Form card**: `background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;`
- **Label column**: `flex: 0 0 152px; background: var(--bg); border-right: 1px solid var(--border);` — always darker than the row
- **Row height**: Fixed `min-height: 48px; max-height: 74px; overflow: hidden;`
- **Labels**: Sentence-case (NOT all-caps), `font-size: 0.76rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-muted);`
- **Row focus**: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 8%, var(--surface))`

## Form Controls

```css
/* All inputs and selects */
background: var(--bg);
border: 1px solid var(--border);
color: var(--text);
border-radius: 5px;
padding: 6px 10px;

/* Hover */
border-color: var(--primary);

/* Focus */
border-color: var(--primary);
box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 20%, transparent);

/* Placeholder */
color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.55; font-style: italic;
```

**Custom select arrows** — always use `appearance: none` + SVG arrow. Never rely on native browser dropdown arrows (inconsistent across OS/theme).

## Layout Rules

- **Inline controls** (input + optional hint beside it): use `flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start;`
- **Stacked controls** (input + sub-hint below): use `flex-direction: column; justify-content: center;`
- **Never use `justify-content: center` in a row-direction flex** — it horizontally centers content, which looks wrong for form fields
- **Controls that are single items** (one dropdown, one short input): always use the inline/row layout so rows stay compact

## Hint Text

- **Inline hint** (beside control): `font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.75; white-space: nowrap;`
- **Sub-label hint** (below control): `font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.7; margin-top: 2px;`
- Keep hints short — one clause, not a full sentence when possible

## Visual Validation Requirement

After any UI change, always validate in **real Chrome** (not headless):

```javascript
const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: 'chrome' });
```

Take screenshots at 1280×900. Check:
- [ ] Row heights are uniform
- [ ] Controls are left-aligned (not centered)
- [ ] Label column is visibly darker than row background
- [ ] Input borders are clearly visible
- [ ] No transparent/invisible inputs
- [ ] Hover and focus states work

## Consistency Checklist — Audit Existing UI

When working in any `.tsx` or `.css` file containing forms or settings panels:
1. Replace any `rgba(0,0,0,...)` or `rgba(255,255,255,...)` used for backgrounds/borders with design tokens
2. Ensure all form rows have consistent height (48px standard)
3. Ensure `justify-content: flex-start` on inline/row-direction ctrl containers
4. Ensure labels are sentence-case (never ALL-CAPS in rendered text)
5. Ensure selects use `appearance: none` + custom SVG chevron

## Workflow Node Config Modals (standard)

All Workflow Designer node configuration dialogs use `WorkflowEditorModalFrame` with class `wf-config-modal` (defined in `src/styles/workflow.css`).

**Chrome (required for every node config modal, including future node types):**

- Interior: `background: var(--surface)` — do **not** lighten the fill
- Four edges: subtle white ring only — border + outer/inset hairlines (see `.wf-config-modal.modal.ram-modal`)
- Title header + Config/Input/Output/Logs tabs stay **outside** the scroll viewport (`toolbar` prop); only the form body scrolls
- Footer Close/Save stays pinned at the bottom

```css
/* Canonical edge treatment — do not invent per-node variants */
border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, white 28%, var(--border));
box-shadow:
  0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, white 14%, transparent),
  inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, white 7%, transparent),
  0 12px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45),
  0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
```

New node configs must reuse `WorkflowEditorModalFrame` + `wf-config-modal` so this chrome applies automatically.
